; EXERCISE 3: PREIMAGES
;
; f is a map from A to B (theory/maps.kurt), and S, T are sets. The preimage of T under f is the
; set of the x ∈ A whose value is in T, `{x ∈ A | f x ∈ T}`. Replace each `todo` by a proof;
; don't change the `show` lines. Check with `kurt 3-preimage.kurt`.
;
; Two sets are equal if they have the same elements ("extensionality"). To prove X = Y:
;
;     let c
;         assume c ∈ X
;             ...
;             c ∈ Y
;         assume c ∈ Y
;             ...
;             c ∈ X
;         c ∈ X ⇔ c ∈ Y
;     X = Y
;
; `c ∈ {x ∈ A | f x ∈ T}` and `c ∈ A ∧ f c ∈ T` follow from each other ("separation"). For a
; union, go through the `∨`: `c ∈ S ∪ T` follows from `c ∈ S ∨ c ∈ T` ("union"), which follows
; from `c ∈ S`. For an intersection, go through the `∧` ("in-intersection").

load theory/maps
const A, B, f, S, T

; (a) The preimage of all of B is all of A.
show f : A → B ⇒ {x ∈ A | f x ∈ B} = A
proof
    todo
qed

; (b) The preimage of an intersection is the intersection of the preimages.
show {x ∈ A | f x ∈ S ∩ T} = {x ∈ A | f x ∈ S} ∩ {x ∈ A | f x ∈ T}
proof
    todo
qed

; (c) The preimage of a union is the union of the preimages.
;     Hint: split into cases with `case` (lesson 04).
show {x ∈ A | f x ∈ S ∪ T} = {x ∈ A | f x ∈ S} ∪ {x ∈ A | f x ∈ T}
proof
    todo
qed
